---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Editorial Team | agediscriminationcalc.com';
const description = 'Who publishes agediscriminationcalc.com, how pages are researched and dated, and how to report an error.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Editorial Standards and Publisher</h1>
  <p>agediscriminationcalc.com is published by The Click Lab Agency LLC, a California limited liability company based in San Diego. The Click Lab publishes a family of plain-English legal and financial calculators; this site covers age discrimination under the ADEA and related state laws.</p>

  <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
  <p>Pages are drafted by the publisher&rsquo;s staff, checked against the primary sources listed on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> (the ADEA, EEOC guidance, and the Supreme Court decisions named there), and dated with the month of the last review. We do not use invented author names or credentials, and no one who works on this site is an attorney. If you want a named professional to rely on, that is a reason to consult one &mdash; the homepage explains where to get help.</p>
  <p>Corrections, questions about how a page was produced, and requests to see the sources behind a specific claim can be sent to <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>

  <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every factual and legal claim is sourced to a primary authority (statute, federal regulation, or published judicial decision).</li>
    <li>Calculator formulas are documented in full on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</li>
    <li>Pages are reviewed and updated when ADEA law, EEOC regulations, or significant appellate decisions affect accuracy.</li>
    <li>No sponsored content, paid placements, or advertiser influence on editorial decisions.</li>
    <li>All content is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. Readers with potential ADEA claims should consult a licensed employment attorney and file with the EEOC promptly to preserve their rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Separately, the case-review form on our homepage is a disclosed paid referral: submitting it shares your information with attorneys who may compensate The Click Lab Agency LLC for the introduction. That&rsquo;s an advertising product, distinct from the editorial content on this page, and it has no influence on the standards above. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for details on what&rsquo;s shared if you use it.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Found an error or outdated legal reference? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> and we will review it promptly.</p>
</BaseLayout>
